          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 4, 2015, around 11 PM, a witness is intrigued by the movements of a bright, orange-red round shape in the night sky. No noise is heard during the observation. The object suddenly disappears. Only one testimony is collected. The observation, at night, of a ball or orange light with movement in the sky in a few minutes, then sudden disappearance, can be explained by a Thai lantern. The change in trajectory observed during the duration of the observation is consistent with the wind's fluctuating direction, as recorded in nearby weather stations on that day (see attached document). The probability of a Thai lantern is reinforced by the presence of a festival in the village that evening, as mentioned by the witness. The GEIPAN GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "09aad1e2aeab12b369222525afff6dda551cbb5185be89d29e5a5b6fd72467a4"
        }
